name tatoeba-exports
# Tatoeba's exports have no header row, and the page on which Tatoeba documents their fields is not on this machine
# (not in the set's directory, not under $LAPLACE_DATA/Tatoeba, not under $LAPLACE_DATA/LaplaceResearch). So no column
# has a name from the source, and none is given one here: a row is recorded as the tuple of its fields, in the row's
# own order, each field as the export writes it (\N and \\ included: what they stand for is not documented here either).
# user_languages.csv is not matched: its last field runs over several lines, which the table reader does not read.
match sentences.csv sentences_detailed.csv sentences_CC0.csv links.csv tags.csv tags_detailed.csv tag_metadata.csv sentences_in_lists.csv sentences_with_audio.csv transcriptions.csv users_sentences.csv
grammar table

claims
row tuple
